From 26e7dd6f59e0a52f90a533d735807f788e941f71 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 23:29:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fence competing spend-stop budget decisions
 atomically

Problem: one spend-stop notice woke creator, observer and shepherd chats; shared default-profile deciders stacked four unconditional last-writer-wins overrides. Producer custody identified only kind=chats, and existing tests asserted one event, not one budget decision. Promote checked unread comments too late to prevent budget mutation.

Countermeasure: under the existing budget writer transaction, compare --seen against the latest committed episode budget comment. Resolve synced comments by portable UID, refuse incomplete evidence, preserve the fence after promotion, and allow deliberate readback reconciliation. Ordinary no-stop overrides retain newest-wins behavior. This does not suppress observer notices or prohibit free-text comments.

Proof: initial regression on main allowed both independent writers (four tests failed). Final consumer run: 48 files,1126 passed,5 skipped; full scripts/check 21 checks passed. Hub read-only replay across all board DBs including sync-shadow: a subset of stop-card rows would require acknowledgment of an existing budget decision (project shadow, default shadow and primary). No production budget changed. Natural post-deploy hold proof and independent exact-head review remain required. Incident and notice row evidence is recorded on the owning card.
